  "homepage": {
    "source": "Blogpage/index.html",
    "path": "blog/index.html",
    "blocks": [
      {
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Sujeet Khadka"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Accidental Game Developer → UI/UX Designer"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Welcome to my portfolio and blog – focused on clean interfaces, intuitive design, and my journey through development & design."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "About Sujeet Khadka"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "I'm Sujeet Khadka, a designer based in Nepal, currently focused on UI/UX and visual design. My work began with a final-year school project and grew through personal experiments in mobile games, small web products, and interface design."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "I learn by making: designing in Figma, building selected ideas with tools like Godot, HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, and using AI-assisted tools to explore and iterate. I am not presenting myself as a full-stack developer; I am a designer who enjoys understanding how an idea becomes a usable product."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Current Focus:"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "UI/UX design, visual systems, interaction design, Figma prototyping, responsive interfaces, and thoughtful use of AI during exploration and development."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Selected Work:"
      },
      {
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Carrom Karrom – A lightweight mobile game shaped by design, performance, and the realities of older devices."
      },
      {
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Nakka – A digital interpretation of a traditional Nepali game, designed around nostalgia, accessibility, and offline play."
      },
      {
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "2048 Dark Mode – A UX-focused redesign exploring dark mode, feedback, undo history, and more comfortable play."
      },
      {
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Online Bus Reservation System – A final-year school project that introduced me to designing and building a larger web application."
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "I am still growing, but the direction is clear: make interfaces easier to understand, more enjoyable to use, and grounded in the people and context they are made for."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Featured Projects"
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Carrom Karrom"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Mobile game with 10K+ downloads. Built with Godot and AWS for online play."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Bus Reservation System"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Full-stack app using Node.js, Flowbite UI, TypeORM, and Figma-driven design process."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Nakka -Nepali Traditional Game"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A nostalgic game project with 1k+ downloads. Designed based on traditional gameplay insights."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "2048 — Dark Mode Edition"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A refined version of 2048 puzzle with default dark mode and user-requested improvements."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Connectum Mobile Game"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This one just has a simple connect-the-dots gameplay UI and Assets which wasn't developed as rest of the games."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Nepali Festive Counter"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A festive counter app showcasing Nepali festivals with interactive elements."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "The Progress Bar np"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A portfolio-style project showcase with a live Netlify build and design-first process notes."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Blog & Insights"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Notes from the projects that have shaped how I think about design, constraints, and usable digital experiences."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Designing a More Thoughtful 2048"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What dark mode, move history, sound feedback, and small interaction details can change in a familiar puzzle game."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Why Lightweight Design Matters"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Building Carrom Karrom around older devices showed me how performance constraints can lead to clearer, simpler products."
      },
      {
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "Bringing Nakka to Mobile"
      },
      {
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "A reflection on preserving the feeling of a traditional Nepali game while making it accessible on a modern phone."
      }
    ]
  },
